#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid "`just` is a handy way to save and run project-specific commands."
msgstr "`just` 是儲存並執行專案專屬指令的好用方式。"

#: src/introduction.md:23
msgid ""
"This readme is also available as a [book](https://just.systems/man/en/). The "
"book reflects the latest release, whereas the [readme on GitHub](https://"
"github.com/casey/just/blob/master/README.md) reflects latest master."
msgstr ""
"這份 readme 也有[書冊](https://just.systems/man/en/)版本。書冊內容反映最新的"
"發行版本，而 [GitHub 上的 readme](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/"
"README.md) 則反映最新的 master 版本。"

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid ""
"(中文文档在 [这里](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/README.中"
"文.md), 快看过来!)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid ""
"Commands, called recipes, are stored in a file called `justfile` with syntax "
"inspired by `make`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"![screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/casey/just/master/etc/"
"screenshot.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "You can then run them with `just RECIPE`:"
msgstr "接著就可以使用 `just RECIPE` 執行這些命令："

#: src/introduction.md:45
msgid "`just` has a ton of useful features, and many improvements over `make`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:47
msgid ""
"`just` is a command runner, not a build system, so it avoids much of "
"[`make`’s complexity and idiosyncrasies](what-are-the-idiosyncrasies-of-make-"
"that-just-avoids.html). No need for `.PHONY` recipes!"
msgstr ""
"`just` 是命令執行器，不是建置系統，因此避開了 [`make` 的許多複雜性與特殊之處]"
"(what-are-the-idiosyncrasies-of-make-that-just-avoids.html)。無須撰寫 "
"`.PHONY` 配方！"

#: src/introduction.md:51
msgid ""
"Linux, macOS, Windows, and other reasonable unixes are supported with no "
"additional dependencies. (Although if your system doesn’t have an `sh`, "
"you’ll need to [choose a different shell](shell.html).)"
msgstr ""
"支援 Linux、macOS、Windows，以及其他常見的 Unix 系統，無須額外的依賴。（不"
"過，如果你的系統沒有 `sh`，就需要[選擇其他外殼](shell.html)。）"

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid ""
"Errors are specific and informative, and syntax errors are reported along "
"with their source context."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid ""
"Recipes can accept [command line arguments](recipe-parameters.html), "
"including [flags and options](recipe-parameters.html#recipe-flags-and-"
"options)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:61
msgid ""
"`just` has a rich [expression language](expressions.html) and many built-in-"
"functions."
msgstr "just 擁有豐富的[表達式語言](expressions.html)和許多內建函數。"

#: src/introduction.md:64
msgid ""
"Wherever possible, errors are resolved statically. Unknown recipes and "
"circular dependencies are reported before anything runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:67
msgid ""
"`just` [loads `.env` files](dotenv-settings.html), making it easy to "
"populate environment variables."
msgstr "`just` [會載入 `.env` 檔案](dotenv-settings.html)，方便填寫環境變數。"

#: src/introduction.md:70
msgid ""
"Recipes can be [listed from the command line](listing-available-"
"recipes.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:72
msgid ""
"Command line completion scripts are [available for most popular shells]"
"(shell-completion-scripts.html)."
msgstr ""
"[大多數常見外殼都有可用的](shell-completion-scripts.html)命令行補全腳本。"

#: src/introduction.md:75
msgid ""
"Recipes can be written in [arbitrary languages](shebang-recipes.html), like "
"Python or Node.js."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:78
msgid ""
"`just` can be invoked from any subdirectory, not just the directory that "
"contains the `justfile`."
msgstr "`just` 可在任何子目錄中呼叫，不限於包含 `justfile` 的目錄。"

#: src/introduction.md:81
msgid ""
"`justfiles` can be organized into multiple files using [modules]"
"(modules.html) and [imports](imports.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:84
msgid "And [much more](https://just.systems/man/en/)!"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:86
msgid ""
"If you need help with `just`, please feel free to open an issue or ping me "
"on [Discord](https://discord.gg/ezYScXR). Feature requests and bug reports "
"are always welcome!"
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:1
msgid "Backwards Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:3
msgid ""
"With the release of version 1.0, `just` features a strong commitment to "
"backwards compatibility and stability."
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:6
msgid ""
"Future releases will not introduce backwards incompatible changes that make "
"existing `justfile`s stop working, or break working invocations of the "
"command-line interface."
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:10
msgid ""
"This does not, however, preclude fixing outright bugs, even if doing so "
"might break `justfiles` that rely on their behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:13
msgid ""
"There will never be a `just` 2.0. Any desirable backwards-incompatible "
"changes will be opt-in on a per-`justfile` basis, so users may migrate at "
"their leisure."
msgstr ""

#: src/backwards-compatibility.md:17
msgid ""
"Features that aren’t yet ready for stabilization are marked as unstable and "
"may be changed or removed at any time. Using unstable features produces an "
"error by default, which can be suppressed by passing the `--unstable` flag, "
"`set unstable`, or setting the environment variable `JUST_UNSTABLE` to any "
"value other than `false`, `0`, or the empty string."
msgstr ""

#: src/requiring-a-minimum-just-version.md:1
msgid "Requiring a Minimum Just Version"
msgstr ""

#: src/requiring-a-minimum-just-version.md:3
msgid ""
"If you use features of `just` which require a particular version, you may "
"use the `minimum-version`<sup>1.55.0</sup> setting to make it an error to "
"use older versions of `just`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/requiring-a-minimum-just-version.md:11
msgid ""
"If `just` encounters a minimum version greater than its own version, it will "
"print an error message with the required version, which is hopefully better "
"than the confused error message it would have otherwise produced."
msgstr ""

#: src/requiring-a-minimum-just-version.md:15
msgid ""
"The `minimum-version` setting should be placed at the top of the `justfile`, "
"before any usage of the new feature that it guards."
msgstr ""

#: src/requiring-a-minimum-just-version.md:18
msgid ""
"Any features which change the lexer in forward-incompatible ways will still "
"produce an unhelpful error message, as the minimum version check is "
"implemented in the parser, which runs after the lexer."
msgstr ""

#: src/cached-recipes.md:1
msgid "Cached Recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/cached-recipes.md:3
msgid ""
"`just` will skip invocations of recipes with the `[cache]` "
"attribute<sup>1.54.0</sup> if it finds an entry matching the invocation in "
"the cache. The `[cache]` attribute may only be used with script recipes and "
"is currently unstable."
msgstr ""

#: src/cached-recipes.md:8
msgid ""
"For example, this recipe will be skipped if `image.jpg` exists and the "
"contents of `image.png` and the output of `convert -version` haven’t changed "
"since the last run:"
msgstr ""

#: src/cached-recipes.md:12
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"\n"
"[script]\n"
"[cache(inputs = \"image.png\", outputs = \"image.jpg\", extra = `convert "
"-version`)]\n"
"convert:\n"
"  convert image.png image.jpg\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/cached-recipes.md:21
msgid ""
"Unlike many other features of `just`, which are, hopefully, well thought-out "
"and user-friendly, cached recipes are inherently fragile. It is important to "
"understand their limitations before relying on them. Please read this "
"section thoroughly, including the friendly admonitions below."
msgstr ""

#: src/adding-and-removing-environment-variables.md:1
msgid "Adding and Removing Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/adding-and-removing-environment-variables.md:3
msgid ""
"By default, environment variables which are exported or unexported in the "
"`justfile` are included in the cache key, and environment variables exported "
"outside the `justfile` and inherited by `just` are not included."
msgstr ""

#: src/adding-and-removing-environment-variables.md:7
msgid ""
"Environment variables can be added or removed from the cache key using "
"`[cache(environment = EXPRESSION)]`<sup>1.59.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/adding-and-removing-environment-variables.md:10
msgid ""
"In this example, the environment variable `foo` will not be included in the "
"cache key, but `PATH` will:"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:1
msgid "Clearing the Cache"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:3
msgid ""
"The recipe cache is stored in a directory named `.justcache` alongside the "
"`justfile`. Deleting it will clear the cache."
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:6
msgid ""
"The cache can also be cleared with `just --clean`, which can selectively "
"clear cache entries:"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:10
msgid "# clear all cache entries\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:12
msgid "# clear cache entries for recipe `foo`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:15
msgid "# clear cache entries for recipe `baz` in submodule `bar`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:18
msgid "# clear cache entries for recipes in submodule module `bar`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:21
msgid "# clear cache entries for recipes in submodule module `bar::bob`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/clearing-the-cache.md:24
msgid "# '::'-separated paths may also be used\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:1
msgid "Friendly Admonitions"
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:3
msgid ""
"`just` will happily skip cached recipes, but it is your responsibility to "
"make sure that this is safe, and that the contents of the cache key capture "
"enough information about recipe invocations for caching to make sense in the "
"first place."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:8
msgid ""
"In particular, there are many details about the context in which a recipe "
"runs that are not captured by cache keys."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:11
msgid ""
"These include the time, input files, output files, system binaries, "
"operating system version, databases, systems over the network, the DNS, and "
"any of the myriad other things which may change the execution of a computer "
"program."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:15
msgid ""
"Attempting to skip execution based on the type of crude heuristics that "
"`just` employs has a long and sordid history. However, it is an undeniably "
"convenient and powerful tool, and it is provided in the hopes that you find "
"it useful."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:1
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:3
msgid ""
"The cache is a directory named `.justcache` alongside the `justfile` and "
"should not be committed to version control systems. It contains cache "
"entries named `HASH.json`, where `HASH` is the BLAKE3 hash of a serialized "
"cache key JSON object."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:8
msgid "The keys of the cache key object are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:10
msgid "`body`: evaluated recipe body"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:11
msgid "`environment`: map of environment variable names to values"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:12
msgid "`executor`: script interpreter or shebang"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:13
msgid "`extension`: script file extension"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:14
msgid "`extra`: user-supplied value"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:15
msgid "`inputs`: map of file paths to content hashs"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:16
msgid "`positional`: positional arguments"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:17
msgid "`recipe`: `::`\\-separated module path to invoked recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:18
msgid "`working_directory`: current working directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:20
msgid "All keys other than `extra` and `inputs` are populated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:22
msgid ""
"Cache key objects for invoked recipes can be printed to standard error with "
"`just -vv`."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:25
msgid ""
"The environment variables included in `environment` may be controlled with "
"`[cache(environment = EXPRESSION])`<sup>1.59.0<sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:28
msgid ""
"The value of `extra` may be supplied with `[cache(extra = EXPRESSION)]`, "
"where `EXPRESSION` is an arbitrary expression evaluated with recipe "
"arguments in scope. Changes to the value of `extra` will cause a cache miss."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:32
msgid ""
"Before `just` runs a cached recipe, it creates a cache key, hashes it, and "
"looks for the corresponding cache entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:35
msgid "If the cache entry is non-empty, it skips the invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:37
msgid ""
"If the cache entry does not exist or is empty, it runs the invocation and "
"writes `{}` to the cache entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:40
msgid ""
"File locks are taken on cache entries, so concurrent execution of cached "
"recipes by multiple `just` processes is safe. If two processes run a recipe "
"invocation with the same cache key, the first will take the lock, run the "
"recipe, write to the cache entry, and relinquish the lock. The second will "
"block until the first relinquishes the lock, see that the entry is non-"
"empty, and skip the invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/implementation.md:47
msgid "The cache can be bypassed entirely with the `--no-cache` flag."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:1
msgid "Input Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:3
msgid ""
"Input files can be provided with `[cache(inputs = FILES)]`, where `FILES` is "
"an expression that is evaluated with recipe arguments in scope and whose "
"evaluated elements are paths. Paths may be absolute or relative to the "
"recipe’s working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:8
msgid ""
"Each input file is hashed with BLAKE3 and added to the `inputs` cache key, "
"which contains a map of paths to hashes."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:11
msgid ""
"Any changes to the contents of an input file changes the cache key, which "
"causes the next invocation to miss the cache and re-run."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:14
msgid "Missing inputs and paths to directories are errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:16
msgid ""
"In this example, the `build` recipe will re-run if `lib.c` or `main.c` "
"change:"
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"[script]\n"
"[cache(inputs = [\"lib.c\", \"main.c\"])]\n"
"build:\n"
"  cc lib.c main.c -o main\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:1
msgid "Output Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:3
msgid ""
"Output files can be provided with `[cache(outputs = FILES)]`, where `FILES` "
"is an expression that is evaluated with recipe arguments in scope and whose "
"evaluated elements are paths. Paths may be absolute or relative to the "
"recipe’s working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:8
msgid "Outputs are not part of the cache key."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:10
msgid ""
"All output files must exist for an invocation to be skipped, and after an "
"invocation runs successfully, it is an error if any output file does not "
"exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:13
msgid ""
"In this example, `build` re-runs whenever `main` is missing, and errors if "
"it runs without producing `main`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:16
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"[script]\n"
"[cache(inputs = [\"lib.c\", \"main.c\"], outputs = \"main\")]\n"
"build:\n"
"  cc lib.c main.c -o main\n"
"\n"
"clean:\n"
"  rm -f main\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:29
msgid "This forces `build` to re-run if `main` is deleted by `clean`."
msgstr ""

#: src/changelog.md:1
msgid "Changelog"
msgstr ""

#: src/changelog.md:3
msgid ""
"A changelog for the latest release is available in [CHANGELOG.md](https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/casey/just/master/CHANGELOG.md). Changelogs for "
"previous releases are available on [the releases page](https://github.com/"
