#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:1
msgid "Selecting Recipes to Run With an Interactive Chooser"
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:3
msgid ""
"The `--choose` subcommand makes `just` invoke a chooser to select which "
"recipes to run. Choosers should read lines containing recipe names from "
"standard input and print one or more of those names separated by spaces to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:7
msgid ""
"Because there is currently no way to run a recipe that requires arguments "
"with `--choose`, such recipes will not be given to the chooser. Private "
"recipes and aliases are also skipped."
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:11
msgid ""
"The chooser can be overridden with the `--chooser` flag. If `--chooser` is "
"not given, then `just` first checks if `$JUST_CHOOSER` is set. If it isn’t, "
"then the chooser defaults to `fzf`, a popular fuzzy finder."
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:15
msgid "Arguments can be included in the chooser, i.e. `fzf --exact`."
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:17
msgid ""
"The chooser is invoked in the same way as recipe lines. For example, if the "
"chooser is `fzf`, it will be invoked with `sh -cu 'fzf'`, and if the shell, "
"or the shell arguments are overridden, the chooser invocation will respect "
"those overrides."
msgstr ""

#: src/selecting-recipes-to-run-with-an-interactive-chooser.md:22
msgid ""
"If you’d like `just` to default to selecting recipes with a chooser, you can "
"use this as your default recipe:"
msgstr ""

