#: src/dotenv-settings.md:19
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-filename` is not set, but `dotenv-load` or `dotenv-required` are "
"set, `just` will look for a file named `.env`, relative to the working "
"directory and each of its ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:23
msgid ""
"`dotenv-filename` and `dotenv-path` are similar, but `dotenv-path` is only "
"checked relative to the working directory, whereas `dotenv-filename` is "
"checked relative to the working directory and each of its ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:27
msgid ""
"It is not an error if an environment file is not found, unless `dotenv-"
"required` is set."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:30
msgid ""
"The loaded variables are environment variables, not `just` variables, and so "
"must be accessed using `$VARIABLE_NAME` in recipes and backticks."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:33
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-override` is set, variables from the environment file will "
"override existing environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:36
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-command` is set, `just` runs it with the configured `shell` and "
"loads its standard output as an environment file."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:39
msgid "This is useful for sourcing secrets from a secret manager or vault:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:45
msgid ""
"The command-line option `--dotenv-command` can be used to set or override "
"`dotenv-command` at runtime, and may be passed multiple times. Each value is "
"run as a command, with variables from later commands taking precedence over "
"variables from earlier commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:50
msgid "For example, if your `.env` file contains:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:58
msgid "And your `justfile` contains:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:60
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set dotenv-load\n"
"\n"
"serve:\n"
"  @echo \"Starting server with database $DATABASE_ADDRESS on port "
"$SERVER_PORT…\"\n"
"  ./server --database $DATABASE_ADDRESS --port $SERVER_PORT\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:68
msgid "`just serve` will output:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:76
msgid ""
"Variables in environment files loaded in parent modules are inherited by "
"submodules."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:79
msgid ""
"Environment files are loaded in submodules<sup>1.49.0</sup> and may override "
"variables defined in parent module environment files."
msgstr ""

#: src/export.md:1
msgid "Export"
msgstr ""

#: src/export.md:3
msgid ""
"The `export` setting causes all `just` variables to be exported as "
"environment variables. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/export.md:6
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set export\n"
"\n"
"a := \"hello\"\n"
"\n"
"@foo b:\n"
"  echo $a\n"
"  echo $b\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:1
msgid "Getting and Setting Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:3
msgid "Exporting `just` Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:5
msgid ""
"Assignments prefixed with the `export` keyword will be exported to recipes "
"as environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:8
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"export RUST_BACKTRACE := \"1\"\n"
"\n"
"test:\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:16
msgid ""
"Parameters prefixed with a `$` will be exported as environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"test $RUST_BACKTRACE=\"1\":\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:24
msgid ""
"You can also use the `[env(NAME, VALUE)]` attribute to export environment "
"variables to a specific recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:27
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[env(\"RUST_BACKTRACE\", \"1\")]\n"
"test:\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:34
msgid ""
"Exported variables and parameters are not exported to backticks in the same "
"scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:36
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"export WORLD := \"world\"\n"
"# This backtick will fail with \"WORLD: unbound variable\"\n"
"BAR := `echo hello $WORLD`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:42
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# Running `just a foo` will fail with \"A: unbound variable\"\n"
"a $A $B=`echo $A`:\n"
"  echo $A $B\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:48
msgid ""
"When [export](export.html) is set, all `just` variables are exported as "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:51
msgid "Unexporting Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:53
msgid ""
"Environment variables can be unexported with the `unexport` "
"keyword<sup>1.29.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:69
msgid "Getting Environment Variables from the Environment"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:71
msgid ""
"Environment variables from the environment are passed automatically to the "
"recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:74
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"print_home_folder:\n"
"  @echo \"HOME is: '${HOME}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:84
msgid "Setting `just` Variables from Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:86
msgid ""
"Environment variables can be propagated to `just` variables using the "
"`env()` function. See [environment-variables](functions.html#environment-"
"variables)."
msgstr ""

