#: src/indentation.md:1
msgid "Indentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/indentation.md:3
msgid ""
"Recipe lines can be indented with spaces or tabs, but not a mix of both. All "
"of a recipe’s lines must have the same type of indentation, but different "
"recipes in the same `justfile` may use different indentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/indentation.md:7
msgid ""
"Each recipe must be indented at least one level from the `recipe-name` but "
"after that may be further indented."
msgstr ""

#: src/indentation.md:10
msgid ""
"Here’s a justfile with a recipe indented with spaces, represented as `·`, "
"and tabs, represented as `→`."
msgstr ""

#: src/indentation.md:13
msgid ""
"```justfile\n"
"[windows]\n"
"set shell := [\"pwsh\", \"-NoLogo\", \"-NoProfileLoadTime\", \"-Command\"]\n"
"\n"
"set ignore-comments\n"
"\n"
"list-space directory:\n"
"··#!pwsh\n"
"··foreach ($item in $(Get-ChildItem {{directory}} )) {\n"
"····echo $item.Name\n"
"··}\n"
"··echo \"\"\n"
"\n"
"# indentation nesting works even when newlines are escaped\n"
"list-tab directory:\n"
"→ @foreach ($item in $(Get-ChildItem {{directory}} )) { \\\n"
"→ → echo $item.Name \\\n"
"→ }\n"
"→ @echo \"\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:1
msgid "Multi-Line Constructs"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:3
msgid ""
"Recipes without an initial shebang are evaluated and run line-by-line, which "
"means that multi-line constructs probably won’t do what you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:6
msgid "For example, with the following `justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:15
msgid ""
"The extra leading whitespace before the second line of the `conditional` "
"recipe will produce a parse error:"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:26
msgid ""
"To work around this, you can write conditionals on one line, escape newlines "
"with slashes, or add a shebang to your recipe. Some examples of multi-line "
"constructs are provided for reference."
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:30
msgid "`if` statements"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:52
msgid "`for` loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:74
msgid "`while` loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:96
msgid "Outside Recipe Bodies"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:98
msgid "Parenthesized expressions can span multiple lines:"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:122
msgid ""
"Lines ending with a backslash continue on to the next line as if the lines "
"were joined by whitespace<sup>1.15.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/multi-line-constructs.md:144
msgid ""
"Backslash line continuations can also be used in interpolations. The line "
"following the backslash must be indented."
