#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:1
msgid "Avoiding Argument Splitting"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:3
msgid "Given this `justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:10
msgid "The following command will create two files, `some` and `argument.txt`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:12
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just foo \"some argument.txt\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:16
msgid ""
"The user’s shell will parse `\"some argument.txt\"` as a single argument, "
"but when `just` replaces `touch {{argument}}` with `touch some "
"argument.txt`, the quotes are not preserved, and `touch` will receive two "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:20
msgid ""
"There are a few ways to avoid this: quoting, positional arguments, and "
"exported arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:23
msgid "Quoting"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:25
msgid "Quotes can be added around the `{{argument}}` interpolation:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:32
msgid ""
"This preserves `just`’s ability to catch variable name typos before running, "
"for example if you were to write `{{argument}}`, but will not do what you "
"want if the value of `argument` contains single quotes."
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:36
msgid "Positional Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:38
msgid ""
"The `positional-arguments` setting causes all arguments to be passed as "
"positional arguments, allowing them to be accessed with `$1`, `$2`, …, and "
"`$@`, which can then be double-quoted to avoid further splitting by the "
"shell:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:42
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set positional-arguments\n"
"\n"
"foo argument:\n"
"  touch \"$1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:49
msgid ""
"This defeats `just`’s ability to catch typos, for example if you type `$2` "
"instead of `$1`, but works for all possible values of `argument`, including "
"those with double quotes."
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:53
msgid "Exported Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:55
msgid "All arguments are exported when the `export` setting is set:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:57
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set export\n"
"\n"
"foo argument:\n"
"  touch \"$argument\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:64
msgid "Or individual arguments may be exported by prefixing them with `$`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:66
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo $argument:\n"
"  touch \"$argument\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/avoiding-argument-splitting.md:71
msgid ""
"This defeats `just`’s ability to catch typos, for example if you type "
"`$argument`, but works for all possible values of `argument`, including "
"those with double quotes."
msgstr ""

