#: src/functions.md:3
msgid "System Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:5
msgid ""
"`arch()` — Instruction set architecture. Possible values are: `\"aarch64\"`, "
"`\"arm\"`, `\"asmjs\"`, `\"hexagon\"`, `\"mips\"`, `\"msp430\"`, "
"`\"powerpc\"`, `\"powerpc64\"`, `\"s390x\"`, `\"sparc\"`, `\"wasm32\"`, "
"`\"x86\"`, `\"x86_64\"`, and `\"xcore\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:9
msgid "`num_cpus()`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Number of logical CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:10
msgid ""
"`os()` — Operating system. Possible values are: `\"android\"`, `\"bitrig\"`, "
"`\"dragonfly\"`, `\"emscripten\"`, `\"freebsd\"`, `\"haiku\"`, `\"ios\"`, "
"`\"linux\"`, `\"macos\"`, `\"netbsd\"`, `\"openbsd\"`, `\"solaris\"`, and "
"`\"windows\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:13
msgid ""
"`os_family()` — Operating system family; possible values are: `\"unix\"` and "
"`\"windows\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:16 src/functions.md:220
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"system-info:\n"
"  @echo \"This is an {{arch()}} machine.\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:28
msgid ""
"The `os_family()` function can be used to create cross-platform `justfile`s "
"that work on various operating systems. For an example, see [cross-"
"platform.just](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/examples/cross-"
"platform.just) file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:33
msgid "External Commands"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:35
msgid ""
"`shell(command, args...)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> returns the standard output of "
"shell script `command` with zero or more positional arguments `args`. The "
"shell used to interpret `command` is the same shell that is used to evaluate "
"recipe lines, and can be changed with `set shell := […]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:40
msgid ""
"`command` is passed as the first argument, so if the command is `'echo $@'`, "
"the full command line, with the default shell command `sh -cu` and `args` "
"`'foo'` and `'bar'` will be:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:48
msgid ""
"This is so that `$@` works as expected, and `$1` refers to the first "
"argument. `$@` does not include the first positional argument, which is "
"expected to be the name of the program being run."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:52
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# arguments can be variables or expressions\n"
"file := '/sys/class/power_supply/BAT0/status'\n"
"bat0stat := shell('cat $1', file)\n"
"\n"
"# commands can be variables or expressions\n"
"command := 'wc -l'\n"
"output := shell(command + ' \"$1\"', 'main.c')\n"
"\n"
"# arguments referenced by the shell command must be used\n"
"empty := shell('echo', 'foo')\n"
"full := shell('echo $1', 'foo')\n"
"error := shell('echo $1')\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:67
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# Using python as the shell. Since `python -c` sets `sys.argv[0]` to `'-"
"c'`,\n"
"# the first \"real\" positional argument will be `sys.argv[2]`.\n"
"set shell := [\"python3\", \"-c\"]\n"
"olleh := shell('import sys; print(sys.argv[2][::-1])', 'hello')\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:76
msgid ""
"`env(key)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable with name "
"`key`, aborting if it is not present."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:79
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"home_dir := env('HOME')\n"
"\n"
"test:\n"
"  echo \"{{home_dir}}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:91
msgid ""
"`env(key, default)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable "
"with name `key`, returning `default` if it is not present."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:93
msgid "`env_var(key)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:94
msgid ""
"`env_var_or_default(key, default)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key, "
"default)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:96
msgid "Executables"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:98
msgid ""
"`require(name)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> — Search directories in the `PATH` "
"environment variable for the executable `name` and return its full path, or "
"halt with an error if no executable with `name` exists."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:102
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"bash := require(\"bash\")\n"
"\n"
"@test:\n"
"    echo \"bash: '{{bash}}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:114
msgid ""
"`which(name)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> — Search directories in the `PATH` "
"environment variable for the executable `name` and return its full path, or "
"the empty list if not found. Requires `set lists`<sup>1.53.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:118
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"bosh := which(\"bosh\")\n"
"\n"
"@test:\n"
"    echo \"bosh: '{{bosh}}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

