#: src/functions.md:278
msgid "`uppercamelcase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `UpperCamelCase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:279
msgid "`uppercase(s)` - Convert `s` to uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:281
msgid "Path Manipulation"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:283
msgid "Fallible"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:285
msgid ""
"`absolute_path(path)` - Absolute path to relative `path` in the working "
"directory. `absolute_path(\"./bar.txt\")` in directory `/foo` is `/foo/"
"bar.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:288
msgid ""
"`canonicalize(path)`<sup>1.24.0</sup> - Canonicalize `path` by resolving "
"symlinks and removing `.`, `..`, and extra `/`s where possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:290
msgid ""
"`extension(path)` - Extension of `path`. `extension(\"/foo/bar.txt\")` is "
"`txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:292
msgid ""
"`file_name(path)` - File name of `path` with any leading directory "
"components removed. `file_name(\"/foo/bar.txt\")` is `bar.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:294
msgid ""
"`file_stem(path)` - File name of `path` without extension. `file_stem(\"/foo/"
"bar.txt\")` is `bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:296
msgid ""
"`parent_directory(path)` - Parent directory of `path`. `parent_directory(\"/"
"foo/bar.txt\")` is `/foo`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:298
msgid ""
"`without_extension(path)` - `path` without extension. `without_extension(\"/"
"foo/bar.txt\")` is `/foo/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:301
msgid ""
"These functions can fail, for example if a path does not have an extension, "
"which will halt execution."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:304
msgid "Infallible"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:306
msgid ""
"`clean(path)` - Simplify `path` by removing extra path separators, "
"intermediate `.` components, and `..` where possible. `clean(\"foo//bar\")` "
"is `foo/bar`, `clean(\"foo/..\")` is `.`, `clean(\"foo/./bar\")` is `foo/"
"bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:309
msgid ""
"`join(a, b…)` - _This function uses `/` on Unix and `\\` on Windows, which "
"can lead to unwanted behavior. The `/` operator, e.g., `a / b`, which always "
"uses `/`, should be considered as a replacement unless `\\`s are "
"specifically desired on Windows._ Join path `a` with path `b`. `join(\"foo/"
"bar\", \"baz\")` is `foo/bar/baz`. Accepts two or more arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:315
msgid "Filesystem Access"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:317
msgid ""
"`path_exists(path)` - Returns the string `true` if the path points at an "
"existing entity and the string `false` otherwise. Traverses symbolic links, "
"and returns the string `false` if the path is inaccessible or points to a "
"broken symlink."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:321
msgid ""
"`read(path)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> - Returns the content of file at `path` as a "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:324
msgid "Assertions and Error Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:326
msgid ""
"`assert(CONDITION, EXPRESSION)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Error with message "
"`EXPRESSION` if `CONDITION` is false. `EXPRESSION` may be "
"omitted<sup>1.53.0</sup>,"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:329
msgid "`error(message)` - Abort execution and report error `message` to user."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:331
msgid "UUID and Hash Generation"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:333
msgid ""
"`blake3(string)`<sup>1.25.0</sup> - Return [BLAKE3](https://github.com/"
"BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/) hash of `string` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:334
msgid ""
"`blake3_file(path)`<sup>1.25.0</sup> - Return [BLAKE3](https://github.com/"
"BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/) hash of file at `path` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:336
msgid ""
"`sha256(string)` - Return the SHA-256 hash of `string` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:337
msgid ""
"`sha256_file(path)` - Return SHA-256 hash of file at `path` as hexadecimal "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:339
msgid "`uuid()` - Generate a random version 4 UUID."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:341
msgid "Random"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:343
msgid ""
"`choose(n, alphabet)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Generate a string of `n` randomly "
"selected characters from `alphabet`, which may not contain repeated "
"characters. For example, `choose('64', HEX)` will generate a random 64-"
"character lowercase hex string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:348
msgid "Datetime"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:350
msgid "`datetime(format)`<sup>1.30.0</sup> - Return local time with `format`."
