#: src/working-directory.md:1
msgid "Working Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:3
msgid ""
"By default, recipes run with the working directory set to the directory that "
"contains the `justfile`."
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:6
msgid ""
"The `[no-cd]` attribute can be used to make recipes run with the working "
"directory set to the directory in which `just` was invoked."
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:26
msgid ""
"Note that this does not affect dotenv file search, or the working directory "
"of backtick and `shell()` invocations."
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:29
msgid ""
"Use `set no-cd`<sup>1.51.0</sup> to make all recipes in the current module "
"default to the same behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:32
msgid ""
"`set no-cd` and `set working-directory` can be overridden on a per-recipe "
"basis with the `[no-cd]` and `[working-directory]` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:35
msgid ""
"You can override the working directory for all recipes with `set working-"
"directory := '…'`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:52
msgid ""
"You can override the working directory for a specific recipe with the "
"`working-directory` attribute<sup>1.38.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/working-directory.md:68
msgid ""
"The argument to the `working-directory` setting or `working-directory` "
"attribute may be an expression<sup>1.51.0</sup> whose value is absolute or "
"relative. If it is relative it is interpreted relative to the default "
"working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:1
msgid "Changing the Working Directory in a Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:3
msgid ""
"Each recipe line is executed by a new shell, so if you change the working "
"directory on one line, it won’t have an effect on later lines:"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:13
msgid ""
"There are a couple ways around this. One is to call `cd` on the same line as "
"the command you want to run:"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:21
msgid ""
"The other is to use a shebang recipe. Shebang recipe bodies are extracted "
"and run as scripts, so a single shell instance will run the whole thing, and "
"thus a `cd` on one line will affect later lines, just like a shell script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/disabling-changing-directory.md:1
msgid "Disabling Changing Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/disabling-changing-directory.md:3
msgid ""
"`just` normally executes recipes with the current directory set to the "
"directory that contains the `justfile`. This can be disabled using the `[no-"
"cd]` attribute<sup>1.9.0</sup>. This can be used to create recipes which use "
"paths relative to the invocation directory, or which operate on the current "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/disabling-changing-directory.md:9
msgid "For example, this `commit` recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/disabling-changing-directory.md:18
msgid ""
"Can be used with paths that are relative to the current directory, because "
"`[no-cd]` prevents `just` from changing the current directory when executing "
"`commit`."
msgstr ""

